    "\n\nSmart thinking. The right approach is a two-pass extraction:\n\n1. **First pass: text extraction** (pypdf) - fast, free, handles text-based PDFs\n2. **Second pass: vision LLM** - only for pages where text extraction came back empty or near-empty\n\nThis way a document with 10 pages where 8 have text and 2 are scanned images would get text extraction for the 8 and vision LLM for the 2. You never double-process and you only pay for the pages that actually need it.\n\nThe architecture would be:\n\n```\nPDF page → extract text → got text? → use it\n                        → empty?   → send page image to vision LLM → use that text\n```\n\nI can stub this out now with a clean interface so your vision LLM project can plug in later. The key is the extraction pipeline needs to work per-page, not per-document. Let me refactor:\n[Tool uses: fs_read]",
